&lt;li&gt;Expertise in software architecture and implementation, with a strong development background in a language like &lt;strong&gt;Java, Python, or C++&lt;/strong&gt;, and significant experience with frameworks such as &lt;strong&gt;Spring, React.js, or Node.js&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong grasp of software engineering designs, principles, and practices, with a focus on building scalable and maintainable systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong communication skills and can distill complex concepts into simple, easy to understand narratives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and implementing internationalization and localization strategies for large-scale enterprise applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, specialized knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;Unicode, ISO standards, and localization frameworks&lt;/strong&gt;, with a proven track record of applying this knowledge to solve complex, company-wide globalization challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with globalization tooling and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building &lt;strong&gt;accessible&lt;/strong&gt; UIs and driving WCAG 2.2 Level AA compliance at scale, including tooling and methodology (automated checks, CI gating, accessible component libraries, and accessibility conformance reporting (VPAT/ACR)).&lt;/li&gt;
