&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everpure (NYSE: P) has evolved from storage pioneer to data platform, closing fiscal 2026 with $3.7 billion in revenue, its first billion-dollar quarter, and accelerating growth into FY27. Our strategic agenda spans the companies defining the next era of technology - hyperscalers, AI labs, the AI hardware supply chain, data platform providers, and the broader AI ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The FlashBlade team builds the industry’s most innovative, high-performance, and highly available portfolio of products that are designed for the most demanding mission critical applications.&amp;nbsp; While we deliver a hardware storage array, over 90% of our engineering staff are software engineers. Our customers are the most important part of our business and they love FlashBlade for its simplicity of management, the constant flow of new and exciting upgrades, and ability to live on the cutting edge of technology while never taking downtime, ever. FlashBlade enables our customers to leverage the agility of the public cloud for both traditional IT and cloud-native applications. You’ll architect, implement, and optimize core services that span on-premises arrays and cloud deployments—delivering seamless storage experiences to enterprises around the globe. If you thrive on solving hard problems, influencing technical direction, and driving innovation end-to-end, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: garamond, times new roman, serif;&quot;&gt;WHAT YOU AND YOUR TEAM WILL BE DOING…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: garamond, times new roman, serif;&quot;&gt;· Own the platform software architecture for New Product Introduction (NPI) programs across FlashArray and FlashBlade, from concept and ERD/PRD review through bring-up, validation, manufacturing handoff and GA.&lt;br&gt;· Define and drive the platform security architecture, including Platform Root of Trust (PRoT), UEFI Secure Boot, Platform Firmware Resilience (PFR), TPM, measured boot, device identity and attestation, and boot drive encryption.&lt;br&gt;· Extend the secure boot chain of trust across firmware, bootloaders, kernel, Purity software and devices (BMC, NICs, HBAs, drives). Work with the security team on key management, the signing infrastructure and the production vs. development provisioning flows.&lt;br&gt;· Drive the post-quantum cryptography (PQC) readiness roadmap for platform firmware and boot, and keep us aligned with industry frameworks such as OCP Security / SAFE, NIST SP 800-193 and NIST SSDF.&lt;br&gt;· Architect secure, resilient firmware update and lifecycle flows: fw_update_tool, factory images, manufacturing provisioning and lock, RMA and re-provisioning, and non-disruptive hardware upgrades.&lt;br&gt;· Lead early hardware bring-up and debug for new CPUs, chipsets, PCIe switches, NICs and add-in cards. Partner with silicon vendors (Intel, AMD, Broadcom, Marvell and others) and with ODM/JDM partners.&lt;br&gt;· Shape the long-term direction for unifying hardware-adjacent management layers (chassis manager, HAL, BMC interfaces) across FlashArray and FlashBlade.&lt;br&gt;· Review hardware designs, ERDs and requirements so that platform software, diagnostics and manageability are designed in from day one, not bolted on later.&lt;br&gt;· Work with BMC Firmware, Kernel IO, Diags, Systems Networking, Hardware, Manufacturing, Security and Program Management teams in Bengaluru, Silicon Valley and Prague.&lt;br&gt;· Own root-cause analysis for the hardest platform, boot and security escalations, from internal test through customer field issues.&lt;br&gt;· Write the design documents and architectural reviews that set standards for the org. Mentor senior engineers and raise the technical bar across teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: garamond, times new roman, serif;&quot;&gt;WHAT YOU’LL NEED TO BRING TO THIS ROLE...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: garamond, times new roman, serif;&quot;&gt;· 15+ years of experience in platform, system or firmware software for servers, storage, networking or other enterprise systems.&lt;br&gt;· A proven track record as the technical lead or architect on multiple NPI programs taken from bring-up to production.&lt;br&gt;· Deep, hands-on expertise in platform security: UEFI Secure Boot, hardware root of trust, TPM 2.0, measured boot, and code-signing and key-management workflows. Experience with Intel PFR, Caliptra, OpenTitan or a similar RoT is a strong plus.&lt;br&gt;· Strong understanding of the x86 boot flow (BIOS/UEFI, bootloaders, Linux kernel boot), plus experience working with BIOS vendors and silicon reference code.&lt;br&gt;· Solid knowledge of BMC and out-of-band management (IPMI, Redfish, PLDM, MCTP, SPDM).&lt;br&gt;· Strong knowledge of hardware interfaces and system architecture: PCIe Gen5/Gen6, I2C/SMBus, SPI, eSPI, CPLD/FPGA interactions, CPU/NUMA architecture.&lt;br&gt;· Strong Linux systems programming and kernel/driver experience. Expert-level C, plus proficiency in Python and shell.&lt;br&gt;· Excellent debugging skills across hardware/software boundaries using JTAG, logic and protocol analyzers, serial consoles, crash dumps and boot logs.&lt;br&gt;· Experience working directly with silicon vendors, ODM/JDM partners and manufacturing teams.&lt;br&gt;· Proven ability to lead and influence through technical credibility across distributed teams without direct authority.&lt;br&gt;· Bachelor’s or higher in Computer Science, Computer Engineering or Electrical Engineering.&lt;br&gt;· Good to have: knowledge of PQC algorithms and migration, Common Criteria / FIPS certification, OCP standards, and ARM-based platforms.&lt;br&gt;· Storage experience is desirable but not required.&lt;br&gt;· You are flexible, accountable and a strong communicator who thrives in a globally distributed team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quo