&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Data Platform team builds and operates systems that centralize all of Coinbase&#39;s internal and third-party data, so teams across the company can access, process, and transform it for analytics, machine learning, and end-user experiences. As a senior engineer, you will work across the full stack of our systems: foundational processing and storage, scalable pipelines, and the frameworks and internal tools that make data easy to use.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate foundational data services, including storage (cloud warehouse, data lake), orchestration (Airflow), batch processing (Spark, SQL), and streaming (Kafka).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain data integration and processing SDKs used by internal services and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design self-service tools so users can manage and troubleshoot their own data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build services for data security, observability, quality, cataloging, and lineage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn requests from analysts, ML, and security teams into reusable, scalable patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in software engineering, including senior-level ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python, Go, or Java backend development skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with data systems or data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with design patterns such as scale-out, caching, key/value, and columnar storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SQL and Airflow for operational data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
